[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Englund Gambit"]
[Variation "4.Nbd2 Nxe5"]
[ECO "A40"]
[Character "gambit,solid"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "development-lead,central-control"]

1. d4 e5 2. dxe5 Nc6 3. Nf3 Qe7 4. Nbd2?! { A quiet developing move that avoids all the tricks. } 4... Nxe5 { Takes the pawn back with the knight. Taking with the queen would lose it, because the knight on f3 would capture it. [%cal Gc6e5] }
5. Nxe5 5... Qxe5 { Now the queen recaptures safely, because nothing attacks e5 any more. Material is level. } 6. e3 6... Nf6 { Develops and gets ready for ...d5, which takes a share of the centre. }
7. Nf3 7... Qe7 { The knight attacked the queen, so she steps back to a safe square. } 8. Bd3 8... d5 { Takes a share of the centre, so Black is fully equal. } 9. O-O 9... Bg4 { Pins the knight on f3 to the queen on d1. } 10. h3 10... Bh5 { Keeps the pin by retreating along the diagonal. } 11. b3 11... O-O-O 12. Bb2 *
